# Low Water, Act 2: ruleset additions. Director's file, 2026-10-17. Private.
# The Act 1 ruleset (../act1/rules.lwd) carries over; this adds Act 2's quests, people, items,
# tools, opponents and encounters. Plan: design/ACT2-PLAN.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- people
@char fisk
name: Dorran Fisk
speaker: FISK
faction: trust
about: The engineer who wrote the restrike clause. Speaks in specifications and apologises for adjectives.
walkaway: Ah. Yes. Of course. Goodbye.
interrupted: Forgive me, I have lost my place. As one does.
fightstart: I am an engineer. I am not built for this, is it not.

@char pellow
name: Mrs Pellow
speaker: PELLOW
faction: trust
about: Crake's housekeeper. Has never seen her employer's eyes.
walkaway: The Alderman will be sorry to have missed you. She will say so.
interrupted: Excuse me. The bell.
fightstart: I shall have to scream, I'm afraid. Properly.

@char rook
name: Euphemia Rook
speaker: ROOK
faction: shelf
about: Telegraphist. Remembers every message she has sent and pretends not to.
walkaway: I don't recall you came in.
interrupted: The sounder. One moment. Nothing. Go on.
fightstart: Not in the office. I have to work in here.

@char ash
name: Brother Lumen Ash
speaker: ASH
faction: congregation
about: The Congregation's treasurer. His relic ledger balances, which worries him.

@char hester
name: Hester Gannet
speaker: HESTER
faction: shelf
about: Pip's grandmother; once the Shelf's local clerk. Heard, not seen, in Act 2.
walkaway: Shut the door. It sticks.
interrupted: Wait. The bell's gone on the machine.
fightstart: That was Will's chair. Mind it.

@char sallis
name: Sallis
speaker: SALLIS
faction: board
about: A tide-warden who believes he is collecting for the insurer (the strippers, town version).
walkaway: Mind the step. It's slippy for clerks.
interrupted: Hold up. The boat.
fightstart: Out here, then. Out here suits us.

@char penrose
name: Old Penrose
speaker: PENROSE
faction: lowco
about: A Low Company man with a son who sang at the Brine; goes out with Sallis on the Board's boat.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- quests
@quest a2.wire
name: The Telegraph Book
about: The 18:30 telegram, and its draft.
stage: open: Euphemia Rook keeps a book of every telegram she sends.
stage: draft: The 18:30 telegram had a draft. Someone else's hand is on it.
stage: read: Lamb has read the draft.
done: read

@quest a2.button
name: The Engineer's Button
about: Dorran Fisk's restrike button, and the clause he wrote for it.
stage: met: The engineer came by the coast road.
stage: why: He wrote the clause so that nobody could ever say no one was at the panel.
stage: proved: The button works, and the clause was struck by someone else.
done: proved

@quest a2.ink
name: Crake's Yellow Ink
about: Who struck the clause.
stage: seen: The clause was struck in yellow ink.
stage: hers: The ink is the Alderman's.
stage: said: The Alderman has said so.
done: said

@quest a2.ledger
name: The Trust's Ledger
about: The keeper's wages, "pending a review".
stage: open: The Trust keeps one ledger for three companies.
stage: wages: The keeper's wages stopped six years ago in the Alderman's hand.
done: wages

@quest a2.station
name: The Lamplighters' Station
about: Gorm's book and the books before it.
stage: open: The Lamplighters' station is on the hill.
stage: books: Lamb has seen what the books say.
done: books

@quest a2.bulb
name: The Procession of the Old Bulb
about: The Congregation carries the Old Bulb down the hill.
stage: open: Fennick means to carry the Old Bulb to Mother tonight.
stage: walking: The procession is on the hill.
stage: ended: The procession is over.
done: ended

@quest a2.boat
name: The Boat to the Spit
about: Getting out to the stranded barges at the second low water.
stage: open: Two barges lie on the Spit. Only a boat reaches them.
stage: afloat: Lamb is on the water.
done: afloat

@quest a2.masters
name: The Masters' Complaint
about: Ships that saw Mother green for a year.
stage: open: Three masters want the Shelf's signature on their complaint.
stage: signed: The Shelf has signed, or refused.
done: signed

@quest a2.errand
name: Mrs Pellow's Errand
about: A letter from the hill to the Ropewalk.
stage: open: Mrs Pellow carries a letter nobody explains.
stage: known: The letter is to Hester Gannet.
done: known

@quest a2.relics
name: Brother Ash's Accounts
about: The relic ledger that balances.
stage: open: Brother Ash keeps the relic accounts.
stage: counted: The relics have been counted against Mother's numbers.
done: counted

@quest a2.substation
name: The Second Switch
about: The hill's own power, and Fisk's test.
stage: open: The hill has a feeder of its own.
stage: tested: The button has been tested in the dark.
done: tested

@quest a2.steward
name: Spratt's Bid
about: The Guild's stewardship, on the ice.
stage: open: Agnes Spratt wants the stewardship.
stage: decided: The Guild has decided.
done: decided

@quest a2.ice
name: The Frozen Gutter
about: What the ice keeps.
stage: open: The gutter has frozen.
stage: read: Lamb has read what froze into it.
done: read

@quest a2.copper
name: The Sale of Merrow's Copper
about: Where the copper goes.
stage: open: Merrow's copper is for sale, or under the gully on a cork.
stage: gone: The copper has gone somewhere.
done: gone

@quest a2.typist
name: Tube Minded
about: Who types the Shelf.
stage: heard: The sticking e, through a wall on the Ropewalk.
done: heard

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- items and tools
@item i.draft
name: The 18:30 draft
about: A telegraph form in two hands.

@item i.ledger_page
name: A page of the Trust's ledger
about: KEEPER: WAGES SUSPENDED PENDING REVIEW, initialled O.C. in yellow.

@item i.fisk_spec
name: Fisk's own copy of the specification
about: The restrike clause, unstruck.

@item i.letter_pellow
name: Mrs Pellow's letter
about: Sealed. Addressed to Mrs H. Gannet, The Ropewalk, in a hand that is not Mrs Pellow's.

@item i.candle
name: A church candle and a length of string
about: A slow fuse, for anyone who knows how long a candle takes.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- opponents and encounters
@foe f.stripper
name: A stripper
faction: board
standing: 10
breath: 6
poise: 4
moves: bar, hook_pull, shove_overboard
yields: standing <= 3

@foe f.stripper_lead
name: The strippers' leader
faction: board
standing: 16
breath: 6
poise: 6
moves: bar, hook_pull, rally
yields: standing <= 5

@foe f.zealot
name: A zealot in a bell jar
faction: congregation
standing: 9
breath: 4
poise: 7
moves: shove, hold, jar_break
yields: standing <= 4

@foe f.guard
name: A Trust guard
faction: trust
standing: 9
breath: 6
poise: 4
tool: w.pole
moves: sweep, pin, call
sight: white
yields: standing <= 3
